# Salvi-attack-live.lic
# Bigshot custom attack routine for Salvi (Cleric) against LIVING targets.
# Prayer of Holding (301) -- the opener Salvi-attack.lic uses -- doesn't affect
# living creatures, so this swaps it for Web (118) and keeps the same Condemn
# (309) follow-up. Drop it into a bigshot hunting-commands list as a single
# command:
#
#   script Salvi-attack-live
#
# bigshot pauses itself, runs this once against the target it already has
# locked, then resumes to loot / wander / retarget -- so this does exactly ONE
# attack decision per call and returns; bigshot re-invokes it every pass while
# the target is still up. The moment the target dies -- at any point, including
# mid-hold after Condemn -- the script returns so bigshot resumes and loots.
# Death is read off GameObj status (what bigshot itself uses), not a
# per-creature kill-message regex.
#
# Modeled on Fizzleworth-attack-base.lic's Web-then-DoT shape:
#
#   1. Web (118) -- an SMRv2 attack, recast until the endroll clears
#      WEB_ENDROLL (101) or WEB_MAX_TRIES (3) is hit. Per
#      https://gswiki.play.net/Web_(118): "Web your target before using a
#      damaging SMR spell such as Condemn (309), as they'll suffer a -100
#      penalty to avoiding your attack" -- literally this combo. Landed once
#      per target ($salvi_webbed_id tracker), so bigshot re-invoking every pass
#      doesn't rewebb (and burn mana) once it's already stuck.
#   2. Condemn (309) -- same empowered-evoke-every-EMPOWER_EVERY-casts logic as
#      Salvi-attack.lic, sharing its $salvi_condemn_casts tally (same
#      character, same server-side empowerment counter, whichever script casts
#      it) rather than tracking a separate count.
#   3. Hold up to CONDEMN_WAIT (or the shorter EMPOWERED_CONDEMN_WAIT) for the
#      DoT, bailing early if the target dies or the room fills past FLEE_HINT
#      living targets (bigshot's about to flee -- don't sit still for it).
#
# Stays in stance DEFENSIVE throughout and never goes offensive: Web is
# SMRv2, and per https://gswiki.play.net/SMR "typically stance is not a factor
# for any spell based SMRv2 abilities" -- neither 118 nor 309 carry Lich's
# stance='yes' flag either (unlike, say, Holy Bolt/306 or Minor Water/903, which
# do), same reasoning Fizzleworth-attack-base.lic uses for Energy
# Maelstrom/Tenebrous Tether.
#
# Low mana: Symbol of Mana if known and off cooldown (cooldown-only check --
# never spends deeds), otherwise wave a wand at the target (same wand logic as
# Salvi-attack.lic: fresh/dead containers and wand type from UserVars.op, full
# multi-line LOOK IN so a categorizing container doesn't read as empty, GET by
# a single adjective since GS chokes on double ones). No pray.
#
# OVEREXERTION: casting a spell without its full mana cost in hand doesn't fail
# cleanly -- the cast goes through and hurts you ("You have overextended
# yourself!  You feel yourself going into shock!"). So every cast here is
# gated on the LIVE checkmana against that spell's real cost. TARGETED Web 118
# costs 5 mana, NOT the 10 effect-list.xml reports (that's the
# untargeted/room-cast cost -- confirmed the same way Fizzleworth-attack-base
# hardcodes it rather than trusting the lookup); Condemn (309) is a flat 9,
# same as Salvi-attack.lic. This is a pure mana check -- no mind-%/rest guard
# (bigshot handles rest-on-mind itself).
#
# If a wound blocks spellcasting outright ("You can't think clearly enough to
# prepare a spell!" -- no roundtime at all), fires ;eherbs --spellcast once
# instead of retrying the dead cast, same as Salvi-attack.lic.

# --- knobs -------------------------------------------------------------------

# Targeted Web is a flat 5 -- hardcoded rather than looked up (effect-list.xml's
# 10 is the untargeted cast). Condemn tracks the lookup with its known value as
# fallback, same as Salvi-attack.lic.
SPELL_WEB_MANA = 5 unless defined?(SPELL_WEB_MANA)
SPELL_309_MANA = (Spell[309].mana_cost.to_i.positive? ? Spell[309].mana_cost.to_i : 9) unless defined?(SPELL_309_MANA)

# Web is an SMR attack; the endroll is the `== +N` on its result line. Keep
# recasting until it lands at least this high, or give up after this many tries
# (and remember not to bother again on this target -- see land_web).
WEB_ENDROLL   = 101 unless defined?(WEB_ENDROLL)
WEB_MAX_TRIES = 3   unless defined?(WEB_MAX_TRIES)

# Flat hold in stance defensive after Condemn goes off, letting the DoT work
# instead of instantly re-engaging. The empowered (evoke) cast lands harder and
# doesn't need the same long pause, so it gets its own shorter wait.
CONDEMN_WAIT           = 10 unless defined?(CONDEMN_WAIT)
EMPOWERED_CONDEMN_WAIT = 3  unless defined?(EMPOWERED_CONDEMN_WAIT)

# Condemn banks an empowered charge server-side every N normal casts. Rather
# than querying `spell` every cycle (slow, >2s), just tally casts locally: every
# EMPOWER_EVERY plain incants, the next Condemn is an evoke. The tally lives in
# a global ($salvi_condemn_casts, shared with Salvi-attack.lic -- it's the same
# character's empowerment counter regardless of which script is casting) so it
# survives this script being re-invoked each attack pass.
EMPOWER_EVERY = 10 unless defined?(EMPOWER_EVERY)

# Living-target count past which bigshot is about to flee (mirrors
# Fizzleworth-attack-base.lic's use of the profile's flee_count) -- don't sit
# still holding for the DoT once the room's this full.
FLEE_HINT = 7 unless defined?(FLEE_HINT)

# Wand config is read straight from bigshot's own loaded settings (UserVars.op)
# so it always tracks whatever profile is active -- Fresh/Dead wand container and
# the wand type(s) from the Attacking tab. The "wand" field may be comma- or
# pipe-separated. WAND_PATTERN just checks the fresh container actually holds a
# matching wand; WAND_GET is the noun handed to GET -- a single adjective +
# "wand" (GS chokes on double adjectives like "slender blue wand", so we never
# name the full thing). Container values here are the fallback if the profile
# leaves them blank.
_op = (defined?(UserVars) && UserVars.op.is_a?(Hash)) ? UserVars.op : {}
_wand_tokens = _op["wand"].to_s.split(/[,|]\s*/).map(&:strip).reject(&:empty?)
WAND_PATTERN = (_wand_tokens.empty? ? /\bwand\b/i : /#{_wand_tokens.map { |t| Regexp.escape(t) }.join('|')}/i) unless defined?(WAND_PATTERN)
WAND_GET = (_wand_tokens.empty? || _wand_tokens.first =~ /\bwand\b/i ? "wand" : "#{_wand_tokens.first} wand") unless defined?(WAND_GET)
FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER = (_op["fresh_wand_container"].to_s.strip.empty? ? "greatcloak" : _op["fresh_wand_container"].to_s.strip) unless defined?(FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER)
DEAD_WAND_CONTAINER  = (_op["dead_wand_container"].to_s.strip.empty?  ? "bag"        : _op["dead_wand_container"].to_s.strip)  unless defined?(DEAD_WAND_CONTAINER)

# --- patterns --------------------------------------------------------------

# GS4 shows this when a wound (nerve/head wound, concussion, etc.) blocks
# spellcasting outright -- no roundtime at all, so a naive retry loop just
# burns the whole cast timeout every tick with nothing to show for it.
CANT_CAST_WOUNDED = /can't think clearly enough to prepare a spell/i unless defined?(CANT_CAST_WOUNDED)

# --- helpers --------------------------------------------------------------

# Monster-agnostic death check: bigshot itself never text-matches kill messages
# (they vary per creature) -- it reads GameObj status, which Lich core keeps
# current from the room/combat XML. A dead creature reads "dead" while the corpse
# lingers, then "gone" once it decays or is looted.
def target_dead?(foe)
  return true if foe.nil?
  return true if foe.status.to_s =~ /dead|gone/
  !GameObj.targets.any? { |t| t.id.to_i == foe.id.to_i && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

def living_targets
  GameObj.targets.count { |t| t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ }
end

# Sleeps up to `seconds`, checked ~4x/sec, bailing the instant the target dies
# (hand back to bigshot so it loots) or the room fills past FLEE_HINT (bigshot's
# about to flee -- stop holding still for the DoT).
def hold_for_dot(seconds, foe)
  deadline = Time.now.to_f + seconds
  until Time.now.to_f >= deadline
    return if target_dead?(foe)
    return if living_targets >= FLEE_HINT
    sleep 0.25
  end
end

# Sends cast_cmd and collects every line through the roundtime/resolution
# message (a single dothistimeout match only sees the first matching line, not
# the whole result block). Stops early on CANT_CAST_WOUNDED (never gets a
# roundtime line) or Web's own resolution text.
def cast_and_collect(cast_cmd)
  text_lines = []
  put cast_cmd
  end_time = Time.now.to_f + 6
  loop do
    line = get?
    if line.nil?
      sleep 0.1
    else
      text_lines << line
      break if line =~ /Roundtime: \d+ sec|Cast Roundtime \d+ Sec|Warded off|Warding failed|is rooted in place/i || line =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
    end
    break if Time.now.to_f >= end_time
  end
  text_lines.join(' ')
end

# Web (118) at foe -- recast until the SMR endroll clears WEB_ENDROLL or
# WEB_MAX_TRIES is hit. Landing it (or running out of tries) marks this target
# handled via $salvi_webbed_id so later passes skip straight to Condemn instead
# of rewebbing a target that's already stuck (or whose TD we just can't clear).
def land_web(foe)
  return if $salvi_webbed_id == foe.id.to_i
  fput "release" if checkprep != "None"

  tries = 0
  while tries < WEB_MAX_TRIES
    return if target_dead?(foe)
    return if checkmana < SPELL_WEB_MANA
    waitcastrt?
    waitrt?
    text = cast_and_collect("incant 118")
    if text =~ CANT_CAST_WOUNDED
      Script.run("eherbs", "--spellcast")
      return
    end
    tries += 1
    roll = (text =~ /==\s*\+?(-?\d+)/ ? Regexp.last_match(1).to_i : nil)
    break if (roll && roll >= WEB_ENDROLL) || text =~ /becomes ensnared|is rooted in place/i
    sleep 0.2
  end
  $salvi_webbed_id = foe.id.to_i
end

# Casts Condemn (309) at foe -- an empowered evoke once EMPOWER_EVERY plain
# incants have been logged (then the tally resets), a plain incant otherwise --
# and waits out its roundtime. Costs SPELL_309_MANA either way; the caller has
# already checked the mana, this re-checks against the LIVE value one more time
# right before the cast so nothing slips through. Identical to
# Salvi-attack.lic's version, sharing its $salvi_condemn_casts tally.
# @return [Boolean] true if the empowered (evoke) path was used.
def cast_condemn(foe)
  return false if checkmana < SPELL_309_MANA

  $salvi_condemn_casts ||= 0
  empowered = $salvi_condemn_casts >= EMPOWER_EVERY

  if empowered
    fput "prep 309"
    waitcastrt?
    waitrt?
    return false if checkmana < SPELL_309_MANA   # last gate before the evoke
    fput "evoke ##{foe.id}"
    $salvi_condemn_casts = 0
  else
    fput "incant 309"
    $salvi_condemn_casts += 1
  end
  waitcastrt?
  waitrt?
  empowered
end

# Web (once per target), then Condemn, then hold for the DoT.
def attack_sequence(foe)
  land_web(foe)
  return if target_dead?(foe)
  return if checkmana < SPELL_309_MANA

  empowered = cast_condemn(foe)
  hold_for_dot(empowered ? EMPOWERED_CONDEMN_WAIT : CONDEMN_WAIT, foe)
end

# True if the fresh container holds a wand matching WAND_PATTERN, read from a
# full multi-line LOOK IN. Containers that categorize their contents print
#   In the mail large sack:
#   Wands [20]: a slender blue wand, a copper wand (2), a drake wand (3), ...
#   Total items: 20
# -- while a plain container prints one "In the <c> you see ..." line; a single
# dothistimeout would only ever see the first line, so collect the whole block.
def fresh_wand_present?
  fput "open my #{FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER}"
  lines = []
  put "look in my #{FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER}"
  deadline = Time.now.to_f + 3
  until Time.now.to_f >= deadline
    line = get?
    if line.nil?
      sleep 0.05
      next
    end
    lines << line
    break if line =~ /^Total items:|^In .+ you see |There (?:is|are) nothing|is closed|can't look/i
  end
  lines.join(' ') =~ WAND_PATTERN ? true : false
end

# Tell bigshot to rest -- out of mana and out of wands, nothing left to do.
def rest_out_of_wands
  echo "out of mana and no usable wands in #{FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER} -- resting."
  $bigshot_should_rest = true
  $rest_reason = "Out of mana, no wands"
end

# One wand wave at foe. If neither hand holds a wand, confirms the fresh
# container has one (full multi-line LOOK IN, not a blind GET) and draws it with
# a plain "get <WAND_GET>"; a spent wand (no roll/roundtime on the wave) is
# retired to the dead container. Nothing to wave, nothing to draw -> flag
# bigshot to rest.
def wave_wand(foe)
  in_hand = [GameObj.right_hand, GameObj.left_hand].compact.find { |o| o.name.to_s =~ /\bwand\b/i }

  unless in_hand
    unless fresh_wand_present?
      rest_out_of_wands
      return
    end

    r = dothistimeout("get #{WAND_GET} from my #{FRESH_WAND_CONTAINER}", 3,
                      /You (?:remove|slip|slide|get|pull)|Get what\?|What were you referring to|I could not find/i)
    unless r =~ /You (?:remove|slip|slide|get|pull)/i
      rest_out_of_wands
      return
    end
  end

  fput "stance offensive" if stance != "offensive"
  result = cast_and_collect("wave my wand at ##{foe.id}")
  fput "stance defensive"

  # A wand that fired -- even one the target fully resisted -- still shows a
  # combat roll or a roundtime. A genuinely depleted wand gives neither
  # ("Nothing happens."), so only then retire it to the dead container.
  fired = result =~ /d100|You hurl|Roundtime: \d+ sec|Cast Roundtime \d+ Seconds?/i
  fput "put my wand in my #{DEAD_WAND_CONTAINER}" unless fired
end

# --- main ----------------------------------------------------------------

$salvi_live_target = nil unless defined?($salvi_live_target)
$salvi_webbed_id    = nil unless defined?($salvi_webbed_id)

foe = GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.id.to_i == XMLData.current_target_id.to_i } if XMLData.current_target_id
foe ||= GameObj.targets.find { |t| t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ && t.name !~ /animated/ }

# nothing (live) to hit -- hand control straight back to bigshot, which loots
exit if target_dead?(foe)

# fresh target -> forget whether Web already landed on the last one
if $salvi_live_target != foe.id.to_i
  $salvi_live_target = foe.id.to_i
  $salvi_webbed_id    = nil
end

fput "target ##{foe.id}" unless XMLData.current_target_id.to_i == foe.id.to_i

waitrt?
waitcastrt?

exit if target_dead?(foe)

# Web and Condemn are both SMR-based -- stance doesn't affect either landing
# (see file header) -- so just park in defensive and leave it there. Only
# wave_wand (a bolt-style item, not SMR) steps into offensive for its own cast.
fput "stance defensive" if stance != "defensive"

if checkmana >= SPELL_WEB_MANA
  attack_sequence(foe)
elsif Spell[9813].known? && !Effects::Cooldowns.active?("Symbol of Mana")
  # Off-cooldown check only -- never touches deeds (same check bigshot.lic and
  # Salvi-attack.lic use).
  fput "symbol of mana"
else
  wave_wand(foe)
end
